/P 140 0 R
/E (While this distinction appears legally sound under a narrow reading of the exemption notification, it arguably overlooks the integrated nature of the educational ecosystem, where affiliation is a statutory sine qua non for colleges to admit students and impart education under a university framework. Without affiliation, the very process of admission and examination cannot legally take place, suggesting a functional nexus between these activities. A contrasting and more liberal approach was adopted by the Bombay High Court in Goa University v. Joint Commissioner of CGST \(2025 \(4\) TMI 1056 - BOMBAY HIGH COURT\), where affiliation services were treated as part of the broader educational function of the university. The Court recognised that universities and their affiliated colleges form a composite academic structure, and therefore, services rendered in that framework, including affiliation, should be viewed as incidental to education, and consequently eligible for exemption.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [9 729 0 R 11]
>>
