/P 147 0 R
/E (These rights are integral to the principles of natural justice and must be asserted before the adjudicating authority in the first instance. A more effective approach in such cases would be to file a detailed application under Section 67\(10\) of the Act, before the Commissioner, seeking RUDs and cross-examination, and if denied, place such denial on record. Only in the event of procedural denial or violation of natural justice would recourse to the High Court become meaningful and sustainable.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
