/E (Where both are invoked for the same act of delayed filing, the overlap becomes impermissible. However, where the defaults are distinct, simultaneous consequences may still be legally sustainable.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
638 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (Another important dimension, perhaps underexplored in the case is the jurisdictional basis for recovery of late fee. Section 73 of the CGST Act is designed for determination of tax not paid/short paid, erroneous refunds, or ITC wrongly availed. It does not expressly extend to determination of late fees. Invoking Section 73 machinery for recovery of late fee may therefore amount to a misapplication of statutory provisions, as late fee is governed independently under Section 47.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
639 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (Further, the procedural requirement under Section 46 read with Rule 68 for issuance of notice in Form GSTR-3A to non-filers is a critical precondition before proceeding against a taxpayer for non-filing of returns. Failure to comply with this mandatory step vitiates the proceedings and reflects breach of due process.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
